{{also|Recollect}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leǵ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ML.|recollectus||remembered, composed}}, from {{der|en|la|recolligo||gather again, recover}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|rĕ-kə-lĕktʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹɛkəˈlɛkt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|rĕ-kə-lĕktʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹɛkəˈlɛkt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-recollect.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkt|s=3}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To [[recall]]; to [[collect]] one's thoughts again, especially about past events.
#: {{ux|en|I remember the concert clearly, but I can't '''recollect''' why I had decided to go there.}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|collect}}
* {{l|en|recollection}}

